Q 1 When a deferred callback (Allow's done or Execute's afterRequest) runs after a generation change, the outcome is silently dropped by afterRequest line 299; is this intended deferred-completion accounting behavior or a gap?
Q 2 Counts doc says CircuitBreaker clears Counts on state change or at closed intervals, but beforeRequest increments counts.Requests (line 289) even in half-open before generation validity is re-checked; is that intended?
Q 3 Execute's panic path calls afterRequest(generation, false) before re-panicking (line 237-238); should a panic count as a failure even if the request never returned an error, and is that resolved intent?
Q 4 TwoStepCircuitBreaker.Allow returns a done callback the caller may invoke later or never; there is no source-specified requirement that done be called exactly once, nor any error returned for a late callback affected by generation mismatch — is that unresolved?
Q 5 onStateChange is invoked inside setState while the mutex is held (line 359); source does not specify whether the callback may safely call back into the breaker (e.g., State or Counts) — is reentrancy supported or unspecified?
Q 6 currentState in closed state may call toNewGeneration (line 338) without changing state, clearing counts; does that mean interval expiry silently drops in-flight deferred outcomes via generation mismatch, and is that intended?
Q 7 In open state, currentState transitions to half-open (line 342) and toNewGeneration clears counts and leaves expiry zero; source does not specify whether there is a cooldown or window limiting half-open attempts beyond maxRequests — is that a gap?
Q 8 defaultReadyToTrip uses ConsecutiveFailures > 5 (line 193) while docs say 'more than 5' (line 98); consistent, but the ordering between counts.onFailure and readyToTrip invocation when multiple concurrent failures resolve is not specified beyond generation check — unresolved?
Q 9 beforeRequest returns the captured generation even on ErrOpenState/ErrTooManyRequests (lines 284, 286); since Execute ignores generation on the error path (line 230-231), source does not state whether returned generation on rejection has any meaning — unspecified?
Q 10 Settings.MaxRequests=0 is normalized to 1 (lines 147-148), and half-open rejection compares counts.Requests >= maxRequests (line 285); after a half-open success closes the breaker then reopens, source does not specify how many half-open probes occur across the open->half-open transition — unresolved?
